From ac08925ea8b89a256c047d5949b8b2c2ca8f397f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gianluca Alloisio <giallodue@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 04:35:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fattn: opt-in fused q4_0 dequantization in the tile kernel
 (GGML_CUDA_FATTN_TILE_Q4=1 for 3..16 columns, =2 also for 1..2 columns)

Head size 256 + q4_0 K/V only. K/V tiles are dequantized straight from the q4_0 cache into shared memory (one thread per 32-element block,
same arithmetic as dequantize_q4_0 + float->half) instead of converting the whole visible K/V to f16 in global memory first. The f16 scratch
for these batches is no longer allocated. Off by default.
test-backend-ops perf, hs=256 nr23=6 kv=113408 q4_0: nb=1 1172->680 us (vs VEC), nb=4 2054->1369 us, nb=2 -> 1124 us.
Server, UD-Q4_K_S + MTP, 113k fill: n3 42.89 -> 45.95 t/s, no spec 23.13 -> 26.97 t/s. Not bit-identical to the default path.
